[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   step_156: boundary-radius forward-model scan (result b122).
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   The radial-shell record (step_076, b41) finds the in-cap rotation
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   excess already fully developed at the 8 AU shell and flat outward,
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   while the putative physical boundary sits at ~50-150 AU.  The
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   open question is whether that is a contradiction: a crossing slip
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   injected far outside the observed arc is absorbed by the orbit fit
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   and redistributed, so a fitted angular offset could in principle be
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   present at 8 AU even when the physical event sat at 100+ AU.  This
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   step measures that directly.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   For each dual-leg cohort comet (the step_151 sample) a position-slip
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   holonomy (the realization step_151/step_145 select) is injected into
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   the truth trajectory at a controlled inbound crossing radius
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   R_INJ in {8, 25, 50, 100, 150, 250} AU.  Synthetic astrometry is
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   generated on the REAL observing chain (same MPC epochs, stations and
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   noise floor) and refit with the identical LM/DE440s machinery.  The
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   fitted solutions are then propagated through the shell set and the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   reconstruction error is resolved per shell:
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   d_fit_vs_true_in[s]   all-fit backward leg vs true PRE-slip inbound
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   leg, osc-periapsis separation at shell s
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   d_fit_vs_true_out[s]  all-fit forward leg vs true POST-slip outbound
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   leg at shell s
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   d_legfits[s]          in-leg fit (backward) vs out-leg fit
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   (forward) -- the synthetic analogue of the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   CODE orig-vs-fut catalogue discrepancy
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   If a slip injected at R_INJ = 100-250 AU produces fitted offsets that
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   are already fully developed at s = 8 AU, the observed flat-at-8
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   profile is consistent with a distant boundary; if the offset only
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   develops for s >= R_INJ, the observed profile would require the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   imprint interior to 8 AU.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   Also recorded per comet x radius: fitted element shifts, boundary
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   products (drot, d_in, d_out, daa) and leg disagreement (ddirf), the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   same transfer vector as step_151 -- so the radius dependence of the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   fitted-observable amplitudes is measured on one construction.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 156]   Outputs:
